In the tree view, the current message you are reading is identified by
an ordinal number right before the word "From:". In the left pane (the
tree) every message is identified by an ordinal number within the
thread which corresponds to this number. So finding the current message
in the tree is no problem.

Finding the parent can be a little annoying in highly branched trees,
it's true. But if visually scanning doesn't get you there, and if the
in-text "Patric Mueller says..." doesn't help you find it, then in
extrema you can always view the full headers of the current message,
grab the msgid of the parent from the References header, and do a msgid
search on it.  Perhaps you consider that a pain, and perhaps you're
right. If it bothered me often enough, I might do something about it --
like hack up a Greasemonkey script to give me a "find parent" button.



